\begin_layout Paragraph
6.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Comparing the four plots above,
 i can infer,
 that Markov's bound is worst at predicting the true probability 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{P}\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq\alpha\right)$
\end_inset

,
 while Chebyshev's bound is closest to the true probability.
 The difference in the accuracy of predictions are a result of the progressively tighter assumptions required.
 Markov's bound only requires that 
\begin_inset Formula $0\leq E[X]<\infty$
\end_inset

,
 Chebyshev's bound uses 
\begin_inset Formula $Var(X)$
\end_inset

,
 while Hoeffding's bound requires that 
\begin_inset Formula $(X_{1},X_{2},\cdots,X_{n})$
\end_inset

 are iid.,
 and that 
\begin_inset Formula $X_{i}\in[a_{i},b_{i}]$
\end_inset

 are known.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To calculate the exact probability is the formula for Bernoulli variables:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
P\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq\alpha\right)=\sum^{20}_{x=20\alpha}\left(\begin{array}{c}
20\\
x
\end{array}\right)(E[X_{i}])^{x}(1-E[X_{i}])^{20-x},
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(\begin{array}{c}
20\\
x
\end{array}\right)=\frac{20^{x}}{x!}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Using the formula gives the probability 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq0.95\right)$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
P\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq0.95\right)=\sum^{20}_{x=19}\left(\begin{array}{c}
20\\
x
\end{array}\right)(0.35)^{x}(1-0.35)^{20-x},
\]

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula 
\[
=20(0.35)^{19}(0.65)^{1}+(0.35)^{20}\approx0.00000198\%,
\]

\end_inset

and the probability 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq1\right)$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
P\left(\frac{1}{20}\sum^{20}_{i=1}X_{i}\geq0.20\right)=\sum^{20}_{x=20}\left(\begin{array}{c}
20\\
20
\end{array}\right)(0.35)^{x}(1-0.35)^{20-x},
\]

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula 
\[
=(0.35)^{20}\approx0.0000000761\%.
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

